    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31030" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĭtĭdĭuscŭlus</span></b> ,
			a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. dim.</i> [nitidus], <i>somewhat
				more shining</i> (Plautin.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 2, 84</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĭtĭ-dĭuscŭlē</span></b> ,
				<i>a little more finely, sprucely</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut curer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Ps. 3, 1, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
